<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 source-specific locate the whole from non-unit fractions">
<h2>Recover the whole from a known non-unit fraction</h2><p>These mathematical diagrams are independently authored. The 2021 original gives <strong>zero and the fraction</strong>, and asks where <strong>1</strong> must be. The entire distance to the marked fraction is NOT automatically a whole.</p>
<h3>Original labeled location: 2/3</h3><p>Divide the known distance from zero into <strong>2</strong> equal spaces. Counting <strong>3</strong> such spaces from zero locates 1, to the <strong>right</strong> of 2/3.</p><div role="img" aria-label="Reconstructed fraction bar from zero to 2/3 with 2 equal 1/3 steps and unit mark at step 3" style="display:flex;max-width:600px;min-height:40px;margin:12px 0"><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:2px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"><small>0</small></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#fff;position:relative"><small>2/3</small></span><span style="border-left:2px solid #4c6980;width:2px"><small>1</small></span></div>
<h3>Original labeled location: 5/4</h3><p>Divide the known distance from zero into <strong>5</strong> equal spaces. Counting <strong>4</strong> such spaces from zero locates 1, to the <strong>left</strong> of 5/4.</p><div role="img" aria-label="Reconstructed fraction bar from zero to 5/4 with 5 equal 1/4 steps and unit mark at step 4" style="display:flex;max-width:600px;min-height:40px;margin:12px 0"><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:2px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"><small>0</small></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#fff;position:relative"><strong style="font-size:11px">1</strong></span><span style="border-left:2px solid #4c6980;width:2px"><small>5/4</small></span></div>
<h3>Original labeled location: 11/8</h3><p>Divide the known distance from zero into <strong>11</strong> equal spaces. Counting <strong>8</strong> such spaces from zero locates 1, to the <strong>left</strong> of 11/8.</p><div role="img" aria-label="Reconstructed fraction bar from zero to 11/8 with 11 equal 1/8 steps and unit mark at step 8" style="display:flex;max-width:600px;min-height:40px;margin:12px 0"><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:2px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"><small>0</small></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#d0e7f3;position:relative"></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#fff;position:relative"><strong style="font-size:11px">1</strong></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#fff;position:relative"></span><span style="flex:1;border-bottom:3px solid #4c6980;border-left:1px solid #4c6980;background:#fff;position:relative"></span><span style="border-left:2px solid #4c6980;width:2px"><small>11/8</small></span></div>
<h2>Optional enrichment: locate 3/4 from the given 1/3 point</h2><p><strong>OPTIONAL — beyond required Grade 3 depth.</strong> Copy the 0-to-1/3 interval three times to locate 1. Then partition 0 to 1 into four equal lengths and locate the third one at 3/4. Teacher accepts one correctly partitioned shared line or separate thirds and fourths lines with the same unit scale.</p>
<h2>Student section synthesis</h2><p>Fractions can share a location with whole numbers: 6/6=1 and 12/6=2. The source warm-up's A–D number-line sorting and written explanations require teacher evaluation.</p><p>Original publisher artwork and teacher-gated Cool-down are not reproduced. <a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-5/lesson-9/lesson.html">Original source 2021 teacher lesson</a>.</p></section>